# Rule: Connection Validation at Ticket Intake

Run this check **before Step 1 of ticket-intake** — before the sprint tracking record is
opened and before any gap analysis or doc lookup. A missing connector discovered
mid-execution wastes a full investigation cycle.

## Required connectors per ticket type

| Connector | Purpose | How to verify |
|---|---|---|
| **{{ tracker_label }}** | Fetch ACs, post comments, move status | Auth check / list projects |
{% if has_sql %}
{% for db in sql_dbs %}
| **{{ db | title }}** | DB assertions on dev/staging | `SELECT 1` |
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if has_nosql %}
{% for db in nosql_dbs %}
| **{{ db | title }}** | NoSQL assertions | Ping / list collections |
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if ui_web %}
| **Playwright / Browser MCP** | Browser automation, UI verification | `browser_snapshot` on a neutral URL |
{% endif %}
{% if ui_mobile_ios or ui_mobile_android %}
| **Appium** | Mobile UI automation | `appium_session_management` |
{% endif %}
| **GitHub** | Branch creation, PR operations | List open PRs |
{% if cloud == 'aws' %}
| **AWS** | CloudWatch logs, SQS operations | `aws_whoami` |
{% elif cloud == 'gcp' %}
| **GCP** | Cloud Run logs, Pub/Sub | `list-projects` |
{% elif cloud == 'azure' %}
| **Azure** | Azure Monitor, Service Bus | Subscription list |
{% endif %}

## Minimum viable set to proceed

**{{ tracker_label }}** + at least one DB connector + at least one UI connector (if
the ticket has a UI surface). Document what was skipped when proceeding without a connector.

## What to do when a connector is down

1. Try a ToolSearch — a deferred tool may appear once the server connects.
2. For MCP servers: reconnect via your MCP client (FleetView, Claude Code settings).
3. Re-source your `.env` and retry before concluding a connector is unavailable.
4. If still down: list which validations will be skipped and continue with the minimum
   viable set.

## When to re-run this check

Re-validate connections any time a tool call returns a connection error. A server that was
up at session start can drop mid-session — reconnect and retry before concluding the data
is unreachable.
